  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The famous country Chefland can be represented as a number line. There are NNN attractions in Chefland, among which the iii-th attraction's position is XiX_iXi​, and the time taken to completely explore it is SiS_iSi​ hours. For convenience, we'll assume the time needed to move 111 unit distance is 111 hour.\n\nOne day, Chef decides to visit KKK **distinct** attractions. He wants you to plan the trip, including selecting the attractions and arranging them. In addition, he somehow wants the trip to be as boring as possible.\n\nTo him, the boredomness of a trip is the total time wasted, including the time spent while moving between the attractions, and the time spent in exploring the attractions.\n\nFormally, if you list the indices of the attractions in the order he visits as an array P=[P1,P2,P3,...,PK]P = [P_1, P_2, P_3,...,P_K]P=[P1​,P2​,P3​,...,PK​], then the boredomness equals ∑i=2K∣XPi−XPi−1∣\\sum_{i=2}^{K} |X_{P_i} - X_{P_{i-1}}|∑i=2K​∣XPi​​−XPi−1​​∣ + ∑i=1KSPi\\sum_{i=1}^{K} S_{P_i}∑i=1K​SPi​​.\n\nYour task is to find the maximum boredomness his trip could have.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK - the number of attractions in the city and the number of attractions Chef wants to visit.\nNNN lines then follow, the iii-th of which contains two space-separated integers XiX_iXi​ and SiS_iSi​ - the location and the time needed to completely explore the iii-th attraction.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum possible boredomness the trip could have.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤K≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq K \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤K≤N≤2⋅105",
      "KKK is **even**",
      "−109≤Xi≤109-10^9 \\leq X_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Xi​≤109",
      "1≤Si≤1091 \\leq S_i \\leq 10^91≤Si​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n7 4\n0 3\n1 7\n2 4\n3 9\n4 5\n5 7\n6 4\n4 2\n0 7\n0 10\n0 8\n0 9",
        "output": "39\n19",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The trip with the maximum boredomness is [4,7,2,6][4, 7, 2, 6][4,7,2,6]. The boredomness equals ∣X4−X7∣+∣X7−X2∣+∣X2−X6∣+S4+S7+S2+S6=3+6+4+9+4+7+7=39|X_4 - X_7| + |X_7 - X_2| + |X_2 - X_6| + S_4 + S_7 + S_2 + S_6 = 3 + 6 + 4 + 9 + 4 + 7 + 7 = 39∣X4​−X7​∣+∣X7​−X2​∣+∣X2​−X6​∣+S4​+S7​+S2​+S6​=3+6+4+9+4+7+7=39.\nTest case 222: The trip with the maximum boredomness is [2,4][2, 4][2,4]. The boredomness equals ∣X2−X4∣+S2+S4=0+10+9=19|X_2 - X_4| + S_2 + S_4 = 0 + 10 + 9 = 19∣X2​−X4​∣+S2​+S4​=0+10+9=19."
      }
    ]
  },
